a2c38a3087d2a3d902b44d30d5d6","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"**(1)** The parallel condition is\n\\[\n\\det(\\vec m,\\vec n)\n=\\sqrt3\\sin^2x-\\sin x\\cos x\n=\\sin x(\\sqrt3\\sin x-\\cos x)=0.\n\\]\nOn \\([0,\\pi/2]\\), this gives\n\\[\n\\sin x=0\\implies x=0,\\qquad\n\\sqrt3\\sin x=\\cos x\\implies x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\n\\]\nHere \\(x=0\\) is included under the usual convention that the zero vector is parallel to every vector.\n\n**(2)**\n\\[\nf(x)=\\sqrt3\\sin x\\cos x+\\sin^2x\n=\\frac12+\\sin\\left(2x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right).\n\\]\nThus its smallest positive period is \\(T=\\pi\\). Moreover,\n\\[\nf'(x)=2\\cos\\left(2x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)>0\n\\iff -\\frac{\\pi}{6}+k\\pi<x<\\frac{\\pi}{3}+k\\pi,\n\\quad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\]\nIncluding the endpoints gives the maximal intervals of strict increase.\n\nFinal answer: (1) \\(x=0,\\ \\pi/6\\) (omit \\(0\\) if parallel vectors must be nonzero); (2) \\(T=\\pi\\), with increasing intervals \\(\\left[k\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\,k\\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right]\\), \\(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":204,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":520,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":173}